# Top 3 — Redesign Plan

## Architecture

### Module registration (findFaseModule)
- Top 3 key: `10/05`, group: `10`, skipTrailer: true
- findFaseModule only matches fases >= module key (10/05+)
- Fases 10/01 (trailer) and 10/02-10/04 use normal media overlay
- DisplayView is optional in FaseModule — modules without one use normal overlay

### State lifecycle
1. Presenter navigates to 10/05 → PresenterView auto-persists initial state (phase: 'intro') to PB
2. Display + phone receive top3_state via PB subscription → module views render
3. V pressed → phase: 'voting' → display shows NameWall, phone shows voting list
4. R pressed → phase: 'results' → display shows donut chart

### Display rendering order
1. Check findFaseModule for current_fase
2. If module has DisplayView + stateField is set → check phase
3. If phase === 'intro' → skip module, let normal media overlay play video/image
4. If phase !== 'intro' → render module DisplayView
5. Otherwise → normal media overlay (trailers, images, videos)

### Module state sync
- Display page: syncs moduleStates from currentSession on load + PB subscription
- Player page: syncs moduleStates from currentSession on load + PB subscription
- Presenter page: syncs moduleStates from selectedSession on load + PB subscription

## Completed Changes

### Display (Top3Display.tsx)
- [x] Heading: text-7xl, animated entrance (scale + fade)
- [x] NameWall: staggered entrance (40ms delay per name)
- [x] CSS keyframes injected via useEffect (not module scope)

### Phone (Top3Player.tsx)
- [x] Intro: branded layout (logo band, gradient, heading, media image)
- [x] Voted popup: "Je hebt gestemd."
- [x] CSS keyframes injected via useEffect

### Presenter (Top3Presenter.tsx)
- [x] Removed "Volgende Vraag" button
- [x] R badge + R keyboard shortcut for results
- [x] V badge + V keyboard shortcut for voting

### Wiring
- [x] PlayerView wrapper passes heading + mediaUrl
- [x] PresenterView auto-persists initial state to PB
- [x] persistState exported from logic.ts
- [x] DisplayView optional in FaseModule type
- [x] ZS module: removed DisplayView (uses normal overlay)

## Bugs fixed
- findFaseModule was too greedy (matched all group fases)
- ZS DisplayView intercepted all 07/05+ fases (no stateField)
- Top 3 DisplayView intercepted intro phase (blocked normal overlay)
- Display page never loaded module states on startup
- PresenterView didn't persist initial state → phone/display couldn't render module
- CSS keyframes at module scope unreliable with SSR

